{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790544952,"nonce":"uGhP5J1WPl2d64UA6WIDa+hI7VE=","title":"AOT: a call on a foreign class goes through runtime dispatch","message":"Requested by caribou (caribou issue 9490ae8): a compiled Wren call of a Haxe static costs far more than a compiled Wren static. `Bench.add(s)`, with Bench bound by an import of a foreign module, compiles to wren_call_1: runtime dispatch, then the member's entry wrapper, which reads the arguments back out of an array, then the symbol. A compiled class's static gets a direct call through the AOT class hierarchy instead. Foreign members belong in that hierarchy, their bodies (the receiver-first call of the symbol) as the direct callee, so the call site checks the receiver against the foreign class, calls the symbol inline, and polls the pending-error word.","files":null}]}